---
import KnowByHeart from '../components/KnowByHeart.astro';
import LegacyAnchors from '../components/LegacyAnchors.astro';
import MeterAnatomy from '../components/MeterAnatomy.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import Procedure from '../components/Procedure.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { ZERO_MARK } from '../lib/checklists';
import { GLOSSARY } from '../lib/glossary';
import { DJ_RULES } from '../lib/rules';
import { GUIDE } from '../lib/sections';
import { href } from '../lib/url';

const moved = Object.fromEntries([
  ...GUIDE.filter((p) => p.id !== 'playing').flatMap((p) => [p.id, ...p.sections.map((s) => s.id)]),
  'check', 'myths', 'reference', 'glossary', 'sources', 'model', 'record-level', 'loud',
  ...Object.keys(GLOSSARY).map((key) => `word-${key}`),
  ...['headroom', 'louder', 'limiter', 'videos', 'quiet-file', 'digital'].map((id) => `myth-${id}`),
].map((id) => [id, `/learn/#${id === 'loud' ? 'myths' : id}`]));
---

<Base title="Out of the red: rig setup and clean recordings" description="Set TRIM, read the right meter and keep blends out of the red. Practical instructions for DJs, with setup and fault checks for crew.">
  <PageHeader title="Out of the red" lede="Rig setup and clean recordings.">
    <p>Every set here is recorded. Keep the mixer clean: turning a clipped recording down makes the crunch quieter, but does not remove it.</p>
  </PageHeader>
  <div class="playing flow" id="playing">
    <KnowByHeart title="When you’re playing" rules={DJ_RULES} />
    <p class="zero">(0) is the number the mixer prints beside the first orange light.</p>
    <nav class="quick-links" aria-label="Playing tasks">
      <a href="#trim">Set TRIM</a><a href="#meters">Read the meters</a><a href="#blends">Fix a blend</a><a href="#knobs">Whose controls</a>
    </nav>
    <p class="other-route"><a href={href('/learn/')}>Learn why and practise</a> with optional listening exercises. Setting up or fixing a fault? Go to <a href={href('/night/')}>Crew</a>.</p>

    <Procedure id="trim" title="Set TRIM in your headphones" level={2} kind="Every track" steps={[
      { challenge: 'Channel fader', response: 'down' },
      { challenge: 'TRIM, HI, MID and LOW', response: '12 o’clock' },
      { challenge: 'Track', response: 'in your headphones, loudest part playing' },
      { challenge: 'TRIM', response: 'first orange (0)', note: ZERO_MARK },
      { challenge: 'Channel fader', response: 'up, when you mix it in' },
    ]}>
      <p>Set TRIM by the channel meter for every track. Tracks arrive at different levels; the knob’s position does not tell you the level.</p>
      <p>A lower TRIM setting is fine. Ask crew for a louder room. A clean recording can be turned up afterwards.</p>
      <details><summary>Why this target</summary><p>The XDJ-RX2 manual asks for orange at a track’s loudest part and warns against red. Our first-orange target leaves room for a blend. <a href={href('/learn/#red-top')}>Read the evidence and limits</a>.</p></details>
    </Procedure>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="meters">
      <h2 id="meters">Read the right meter</h2>
      <MeterAnatomy />
      <p>The numbers between the lights are printed on the mixer, in dB.</p>
      <p>Set each deck by its channel meter. During a blend, watch the MASTER meters as well. Lowering a fader reduces that track in the mix; it does not lower its channel meter.</p>
      <p>If a channel reaches red, turn its TRIM down. If the MASTER meters’ top orange lights, use the blend fix below.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="blends">
      <h2 id="blends">Keep blends out of the red</h2>
      <Procedure title="MASTER meters: top orange lit" kind="Fix" steps={[
        { challenge: 'A channel fader', response: 'down a little', note: 'Use the incoming track’s fader. If both are already up, either one works.' },
        { challenge: 'HI, MID and LOW', response: '12 o’clock or lower', note: 'Boosting EQ adds level too.' },
        { challenge: 'MASTER meters', response: 'top orange dark again' },
      ]} />
      <p>Two tracks add together. First orange on each channel leaves room for their combined peaks. Keep the MASTER meters’ top orange dark, even when both tracks are playing.</p>
      <p><a href={href('/learn/#blends')}>Try a blend and see the meters change</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="knobs">
      <h2 id="knobs">Whose controls</h2>
      <div class="whose">
        <div><h3 id="yours">Yours</h3><dl>
          <div><dt>TRIM, HI, MID and LOW</dt><dd>Each track’s level and EQ.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Channel faders</dt><dd>The blend.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>BOOTH MONITOR</dt><dd>Your booth monitors only.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>HEADPHONES LEVEL</dt><dd>Your headphones only.</dd></div>
        </dl></div>
        <div><h3 id="crews">The crew’s</h3><dl>
          <div><dt>MASTER LEVEL</dt><dd>Leave it as you find it. It changes the room and recording together.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>MASTER ATT and BOOTH ATT</dt><dd>The output settings in UTILITY.</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Amp gain knobs</dt><dd>The room’s volume. They face the crowd, under the table.</dd></div>
        </dl></div>
      </div>
      <p><strong>Warning.</strong> A night at club volume can damage your hearing. Keep BOOTH MONITOR and HEADPHONES LEVEL no louder than you need. Wear earplugs: flat-response ones keep the mix clear.</p>
      <p>If you load MY SETTINGS from USB, tell the crew. It may change MASTER ATT and BOOTH ATT.</p>
      <p>For a louder room, ask crew. Turning up the mixer may clip the recording without making the speakers louder. The DriveRack’s limiter is on the speaker path; the Howler records from a different output.</p>
      <p><a href={href('/learn/#signal')}>See which control changes which output</a>.</p>
    </section>
    <aside class="finish">
      <h2>Ready to play</h2>
      <p>Use the meters at the loudest part of each track and during blends. If something still sounds wrong, ask crew and use <a href={href('/night/#fixes')}>the fault guide</a>.</p>
      <p>For practice and explanations, continue to <a href={href('/learn/')}>Learn why and practise</a>. For files after the night, use <a href={href('/recordings/')}>Recordings</a>.</p>
    </aside>
    <LegacyAnchors map={moved} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .playing { row-gap: 1.5rem; padding-block-start: 1.5rem; }
  .section, .finish { display: grid; gap: 1rem; margin-block-start: 1rem; }
  .quick-links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.25rem 1.25rem; border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .quick-links a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 2.75rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .other-route, .zero { font-size: var(--text-sm); }
  .whose { display: grid; gap: 1.5rem; }
  .whose h3 { font-size: var(--text-rule); padding-bottom: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); }
  .whose dl > div { padding-block: 0.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .whose dt { font-weight: 700; }
  .whose dd { margin: 0.1rem 0 0; }
  .finish { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .whose { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
</style>
